      ],
      "id": "zainctu"
    },
    {
      "id": "i8ppxne",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Chemical Reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "A chemical reaction involves the breaking and making of chemical bonds to produce new substances with entirely different properties.",
        "Chemical equations must be balanced to satisfy the Law of Conservation of Mass, ensuring equal atoms on reactants and products sides.",
        "Key indicators of a chemical reaction include change in state, color, temperature, or evolution of a gas.",
        "Oxidation involves the gain of oxygen or loss of hydrogen, whereas reduction involves the loss of oxygen or gain of hydrogen.",
        "Corrosion and rancidity are everyday effects of oxidation processes affecting metals and fat-containing food items respectively."
      ],
      "id": "uuqq0cw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dqy1xyc",
      "content": "• A chemical reaction is a process in which one or more substances are transformed into new substances."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rx6gxhi",
      "content": "• The substances that take part in a reaction are called reactants."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pekwvu8",
      "content": "• The substances formed in a reaction are called products."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bshepfa",
      "content": "• Chemical reactions involve breaking and forming of chemical bonds."
    },
    {
      "id": "st54gd1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Chemical Equation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a5iuv4m",
      "content": "A chemical equation is a symbolic representation of a chemical reaction using chemical formulas."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e56kv1i",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "a09qp9j",
      "content": "2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O"
    },
    {
      "id": "7q4n5yq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Balanced Chemical Equation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ql4c0d1",
      "content": "A balanced chemical equation has an equal number of atoms of each element on both sides."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "feezsb6",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4asqmtu",
      "content": "CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O"
    },
    {
      "id": "bd3lf5h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Indicators of Chemical Reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "A balanced chemical equation has an equal number of atoms of each element on both reactant and product sides.",
      "id": "7si9udn"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4krf4fx",
      "content": "• Change in colour"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "m5c7a0p",
      "content": "• Change in temperature"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "phr0wq6",
      "content": "• Formation of gas"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lnj1els",
      "content": "• Formation of precipitate"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q5wxsi5",
      "content": "• Emission of light or sound"
    },
    {
      "id": "fbwoln0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Types of Chemical Reactions"
    },
    {
      "id": "ea7mz7k",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Reaction Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>General Form</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Example</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Combination Reaction</p>",
            "<p>A + B → AB</p>",
            "<p>2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Decomposition Reaction</p>",
            "<p>AB → A + B</p>",
            "<p>CaCO₃ → CaO + CO₂</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Displacement Reaction</p>",
