          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pomqwqe",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Oxidation and Reduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ecaz1g4",
      "content": "Oxidation: Addition of oxygen or loss of hydrogen."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Parameter",
        "Exothermic Reaction",
        "Endothermic Reaction"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Heat Energy",
          "Released into the surroundings",
          "Absorbed from the surroundings"
        ],
        [
          "Temperature",
          "Surrounding temperature increases",
          "Surrounding temperature decreases"
        ],
        [
          "Common Example",
          "Respiration, Burning of Natural Gas",
          "Photosynthesis, Thermal Decomposition"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "6tk340b"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ngnmr04",
      "content": "Reduction: Removal of oxygen or gain of hydrogen."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "py80h5a",
      "content": "These reactions together are called redox reactions."
    },
    {
      "id": "riacwkv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Exothermic and Endothermic Reactions"
    },
    {
      "id": "qz4yw6b",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Reaction Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Exothermic Reaction</p>",
            "<p>Releases heat energy</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Endothermic Reaction</p>",
            "<p>Absorbs heat energy</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4zx0v55",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Corrosion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hnzq83b",
      "content": "Corrosion is the gradual destruction of metals due to chemical reactions with the environment. Rusting of iron is the most common example."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dgekgw6",
      "content": "Example of rusting:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9dzpj0a",
      "content": "Iron + Oxygen + Water → Rust"
    },
    {
      "id": "7whshd8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Rancidity"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9qlxjml",
      "content": "Rancidity refers to the oxidation of fats and oils in food which causes unpleasant smell and taste. It can be prevented by storing food in airtight containers."
    },
    {
      "id": "fbup9s9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Catalysts"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Respiration is classified as an exothermic reaction, while photosynthesis is an endothermic process.",
        "Rancidity in food items containing fats and oils is prevented by flushing packaging with inert nitrogen gas.",
        "Catalysts alter the rate of a chemical reaction without undergoing any permanent chemical change themselves."
      ],
      "id": "k4igcik"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j44czej",
      "content": "A catalyst is a substance that increases the rate of a chemical reaction without being consumed in the reaction."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "exqqc14",
      "content": "Examples: Platinum, Iron catalyst in Haber process"
    },
    {
      "id": "azznrba",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aj5vx59",
      "content": "• Chemical equations represent chemical reactions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i5au94c",
      "content": "• Rusting of iron is a common example of corrosion."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p5mfgwg",
      "content": "• Redox reactions involve oxidation and reduction."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7gklduo",
      "content": "• Exothermic reactions release heat energy."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}